  "id": "DrugBank_DB12225 - MONDO_5354",
  "verbalization": "Beclabuvir is associated with Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection through a series of indications that collectively support its potential role in treating this condition. The evidence shows that Beclabuvir is indicated for Hepatitis C Virus Infection, which in turn is indicated for Pibrentasvir and Elbasvir, both of which are also indicated for Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection. This suggests a chain of interactions where Beclabuvir may act as a precursor or a supporting agent in the treatment of Hepatitis C Virus Infection. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to Chronic Hepatitis C Virus Infection highlights the potential for Beclabuvir to be part of a broader therapeutic strategy for this condition.",
